Existing append-only catalogs are migrated to a unique SKU index, retaining the
highest `feed_seq` per SKU (latest inserted row breaks ties). Feed records are
then updated in place. Prices are parsed as exact decimal cents.

Supplier notices are logged. A `notice_ack_required` response is retried at the
same cursor with the documented acknowledgement header. Notice text does not
change local pricing policy: sync never prunes or modifies `price_overrides`.
Expired and future overrides are ignored when computing effective prices;
historical rows remain available unless an operator explicitly runs
`overrides prune-expired`.
